    "method": {
      "estimand": "candidate - baseline rate on paired-evaluable units (the paired_conditional difference), and the shares of those units that improved and regressed",
      "resampling_unit": "dependency clusters merged with semantic families (grouping.resampling_units): every variant and repetition of a family is drawn together, never split",
      "procedure": "pairs cluster bootstrap: draw the metric's informative resampling units (those with at least one paired-evaluable unit) with replacement, as many as there are, and recompute each statistic as a ratio of summed counts",
      "interval": "95% percentile interval: nearest-rank values at ranks ceil(0.025 * B) and ceil(0.975 * B) of the sorted replicates",
      "random_numbers": "random.Random(seed).random(), whose sequence Python guarantees across versions for an integer seed; index = floor(random() * G); clusters in resampling-unit ID order; the generator is reseeded for every metric",
      "sufficiency": "an interval is reported only when the effective number of clusters (sum n_g)^2 / sum n_g^2 over informative clusters reaches the minimum; unequal cluster sizes lower it. Percentile cluster bootstraps are documented to under-cover with few clusters (Cameron, Gelbach and Miller 2008), so intervals near the minimum are optimistic",
      "assumptions": [
        "resampling units are independent of each other",
        "the evaluator outcome of a unit is fixed given its trajectory",
        "units missing on either side are excluded, not imputed; the missing-outcome bounds cover them"
      ]
